From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:09:48 +1100
Subject: [PATCH wireless-next 1/9] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: fix the TX power
 estimate table upload

The per-core tables of estimated output power per TSSI value are 16
bits wide, and b43_phy_ht_tx_power_ctl_setup() uploads them with a
16-bit bulk write, but builds them as u32. So the upload takes the
halves of the first 32 values: entry 2k gets the estimate for TSSI k,
every odd entry 0. Closed-loop TX power control, enabled by default,
works from these tables.

On a BCM4331 at 2.4 GHz, close to the AP, fixing the tables lowers the
signal seen by a monitor by 4-5 dB, and the higher OFDM rates start
working: minstrel's success rate at 36 Mbit/s goes from about 40% to
84%, at 54 Mbit/s from about 31% to 60%. The tables read back from the
hardware then match the ones Broadcom's wl driver writes (64 16-bit
entries each, in an MMIO trace on the same card).

Fixes: 5949e0406041 ("b43: HT-PHY: setup TX power control")
Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
index fab8399c64f7..57f80093e9d1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ht.c
@@ -714,13 +714,13 @@ static void b43_phy_ht_tx_power_ctl_setup(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 
 	for (c = 0; c < 3; c++) {
 		s32 num, den, pwr;
-		u32 regval[64];
+		u16 regval[64];
 
 		for (i = 0; i < 64; i++) {
 			num = 8 * (16 * b0[c] + b1[c] * i);
 			den = 32768 + a1[c] * i;
 			pwr = max((4 * num + den / 2) / den, -8);
-			regval[i] = pwr;
+			regval[i] = (u16)pwr;
 		}
 		b43_httab_write_bulk(dev, B43_HTTAB16(26 + c, 0), 64, regval);
 	}

